.SH NAME
dtpcadmin \- Delay\-Tolerant Payload Conditioning (DTPC) administration interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBdtpcadmin\fR [ \fIcommands_filename\fR | . ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBdtpcadmin\fR configures, starts, manages, and stops DTPC operations for
the local ION node.
.PP
It operates in response to DTPC configuration commands found in the file
\&\fIcommands_filename\fR, if provided; if not, \fBdtpcadmin\fR prints
a simple prompt (:) so that the user may type commands
directly into standard input.  If \fIcommands_filename\fR is a period (.), the
effect is the same as if a command file containing the single command 'x'
were passed to \fBdtpcadmin\fR \-\- that is, the ION node's \fIdtpcclock\fR task and
\&\fIdtpcd\fR task are stopped.
.PP
The format of commands for \fIcommands_filename\fR can be queried from
\&\fBdtpcadmin\fR with the 'h' or '?' commands at the prompt.  The commands are
documented in \fBdtpcrc\fR\|(5).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.ie n .IP 0 4
.el .IP \f(CW0\fR 4
.IX Item "0"
Successful completion of DTPC administration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
.IP dtpcadmin 4
.IX Item "dtpcadmin"
Enter interactive DTPC configuration command entry mode.
.IP "dtpcadmin host1.dtpc" 4
.IX Item "dtpcadmin host1.dtpc"
Execute all configuration commands in \fIhost1.dtpc\fR, then terminate immediately.
.IP "dtpcadmin ." 4
.IX Item "dtpcadmin ."
Stop all DTPC operations on the local node.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
See \fBdtpcrc\fR\|(5) for details of the DTPC configuration commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
\&\fBNote\fR: all ION administration utilities expect source file input to be
lines of ASCII text that are NL-delimited.  If you edit the dtpcrc file on
a Windows machine, be sure to \fBuse dos2unix to convert it to Unix text format\fR
before presenting it to \fBdtpcadmin\fR.  Otherwise \fBdtpcadmin\fR will detect syntax
errors and will not function satisfactorily.
.PP
The following diagnostics may be issued to the logfile ion.log:
.IP "dtpcadmin can't attach to ION." 4
.IX Item "dtpcadmin can't attach to ION."
There is no SDR data store for \fIdtpcadmin\fR to use.  You should run \fBionadmin\fR\|(1)
first, to set up an SDR data store for ION.
.IP "Can't open command file..." 4
.IX Item "Can't open command file..."
The \fIcommands_filename\fR specified in the command line doesn't exist.
.PP
Various errors that don't cause \fBdtpcadmin\fR to fail but are noted in the
\&\fBion.log\fR log file may be caused by improperly formatted commands
given at the prompt or in the \fIcommands_filename\fR file.
Please see \fBdtpcrc\fR\|(5) for details.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBdtpcrc\fR\|(5)
